  "id": "Compound::DB00786 - Gene::4319",
  "verbalization": "Marimastat is likely to interact with Mmp10 through a shared pathway involving matrix metalloproteinases (MMPs). The evidence suggests that Marimastat binds to Mmp23b, Mmp27, and Mmp26, all of which are part of the MMP family and are participated by Mmp10. This indicates that Marimastat may influence Mmp10 through a common mechanism, possibly by modulating the activity of MMPs. The high scores in all three paths suggest a consistent interaction pattern, implying that Marimastat's effects on these MMPs may converge on Mmp10. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Marimastat in regulating MMP activity, which could have implications for its therapeutic effects or side effects. The evidence supports a mechanism where Marimastat's binding to MMPs leads to a downstream effect on Mmp10, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
